*> The chunk generation queue (research R12; core/src/gen-queue.cob): chunks wanted by a player's view
*> that are not loaded yet. GQ-BUDGET is the number of chunks CORE-TICK generates per tick (a hosting
*> mechanism, not game behaviour: it changes when a chunk exists, not what it holds); the queue is served
*> nearest first, by the distance of the chunk to the nearest alive player of its dimension.
*> GQ-GENERATED counts the chunks the queue has generated since the world was opened.
 78 GQ-CAPACITY            VALUE 1024.
 78 GQ-BUDGET              VALUE 2.
 01 GEN-QUEUE EXTERNAL.
    05 GQ-COUNT             BINARY-LONG.
    05 GQ-GENERATED         BINARY-DOUBLE.
    05 GQ-ENTRY OCCURS 1024 TIMES.
       10 GQ-DIM            BINARY-LONG.
       10 GQ-X              BINARY-LONG.
       10 GQ-Z              BINARY-LONG.
*> The resumable generation (research R12, GENJOB.cpy): GQ-STEP-BUDGET is the number of generation steps CORE-TICK may run per
*> tick for a standard-pipeline chunk (the steps of GENSTEPS.cpy; a hosting mechanism like GQ-BUDGET), GQ-MS-HUNDREDTHS the most
*> wall time in hundredths of a second it lets one tick spend on them (checked between steps, 0 = no limit; the steps decide
*> what is generated, the clock only when). GQ-JOB is the chunk being generated by steps, one at a time, taken from the queue.
*> GQ-SETUP-DONE is 1 once the density evaluator has been seeded for the open world; GQ-STEPS counts the steps run.
 78 GQ-STEP-BUDGET         VALUE 16.
 78 GQ-MS-HUNDREDTHS       VALUE 1.
 01 GEN-RESUME EXTERNAL.
    05 GQ-SETUP-DONE        BINARY-LONG.
    05 GQ-STEPS             BINARY-DOUBLE.
 01 GQ-JOB EXTERNAL.
    COPY GENJOB.
